CHANGES: I rewrote `/agent/solver.md`. The agent was submitting after only about 3 of its 16 calls, and 19 of the 34 failures didn't even pass the public examples. The new prompt requires:
- a short algorithm plan and hand check before coding;
- a `run_tests` pass on the public examples before any submit;
- a brute-force comparison on random small inputs;
- a timing run on a max-size input;
- submitting only after all of those pass.

I ran `validate()` and it passed. I did not run any trials, so the effect is untested.

PREDICTED_DELTA: +4
